<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Alamannia</h1><p class="st-meta">536 CE – 746 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Frankish duchy that ruled the Alemanni of south-west Germany and Switzerland for two centuries, until the Carolingians abolished it at Cannstatt.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a>' victories over the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alemanni">Alemanni</a> around 496 and 506, the southern Alemanni stayed under Ostrogothic protection until 536, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoth</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/witigis">Witigis</a> ceded them to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a>. The Merovingian kings then placed the Alemanni under dukes, a region covering modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swiss-confederation">Switzerland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia-bavaria">Bavarian Swabia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes governed under Frankish overlordship but often acted independently, especially as Merovingian power weakened. Law was codified in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pactus-alamannorum">Pactus</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lex-alamannorum">Lex Alamannorum</a> of the early 8th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> spread through bishoprics at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstanz">Constance</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-basel">Basel</a> and monasteries such as St Gall, founded on the hermitage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Gallus</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichenau-island">Reichenau</a>, founded in 724.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lantfrid">Lantfrid</a> and his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theudebald-duke-of-alamannia">Theudebald</a> resisted the rising Carolingian mayors of the palace. In 746 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carloman-mayor-of-the-palace">Carloman</a> summoned the Alemannic nobility to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blood-court-at-cannstatt">Cannstatt</a> and executed many of them, ending the ducal office. Alamannia was then ruled by Frankish counts until the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-swabia">Duchy of Swabia</a> emerged in the early 10th century.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-alamannia.jpg" alt="Duchy of Alamannia" width="320" height="270"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alamannien_Hochburgund_ca_1000.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>536 CE – 746 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gotfrid, Lantfrid, Theudebald</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, with surviving paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old High German (Alemannic)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Alemannia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=641&amp;focus=duchy-of-alamannia" aria-label="Duchy of Alamannia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4892 485 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Alamannia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5212 741L5054 728M5212 741L5232 741"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5232 741h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5212 741h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5212 741h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=641&amp;focus=duchy-of-alamannia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
